# Instruction-count benchmark corpus.
#
# One guest per line: a path under build/, then free-form notes.  Each is a
# program already built and validated by check-emu (build/cf, ColdFire) or
# check-rv-emu (build/rv, RISC-V), reused here for its instruction count
# rather than its output.  The set spans both emulator cores and a range of
# workloads from a few thousand to a few million instructions, so a codegen
# or core change that moves work shows up somewhere.
#
# Keep entries deterministic and self-contained (no stdin, clean exit).
# After adding or removing one, run: make bench-accept

# ColdFire (m68k) guests
cf/moo_func                     Moo: function calls and locals
cf/pascal_t052_set_basic        Pascal: set operations
cf/pascal_t135_prime_sieve      Pascal: sieve of Eratosthenes
cf/pascal_t177_deep_recursion   Pascal: deep recursion
cf/pascal_t127_fibonacci        Pascal: recursive fibonacci

# RISC-V (rv32) guests
rv/loop                         tinc: loop
rv/fib                          tinc: recursive fibonacci
rv/scm_reset_heap               Scheme: heap churn
rv/scm_reset_reclaim            Scheme: heap churn with reclaim
